1. Introduction
The Hospital Queue Management System is a Java-based application designed to manage patients waiting for consultation in different hospital departments.
The system replaces manual queue management with a computerized priority-based system. Patients are assigned tokens and served according to their priority.
The priority system is:
1.	Emergency – Highest priority
2.	Senior Citizen (60+)
3.	Normal Patient
The application is completely command-line based, allowing it to be compiled and executed directly from a terminal.
________________________________________
2. Problem Statement
In hospitals, manually managing patient queues can result in long waiting times, confusion, and difficulty in handling emergency and senior patients.
The objective of this project is to develop a Hospital Queue Management System in Java that efficiently registers patients, generates tokens, manages queues, and ensures that patients with higher priority are served first.
