6. Main Features
6.1 Patient Registration
The user can enter:
•	Patient name
•	Age
•	Gender
•	Contact number
•	Hospital department
•	Emergency status
________________________________________
6.2 Priority Management
Patients are automatically assigned priority.
Priority	Category
1	Emergency
2	Senior Citizen (60+)
3	Normal
A lower priority number means the patient is served first.
________________________________________
6.3 Token Generation
Every registered patient receives a token number.
Example:
Patient: Rahul
Department: General Medicine
Token: 5
Priority: Normal
Status: Waiting
Token numbers are maintained separately for each department.
________________________________________
6.4 Department Management
The system supports departments such as:
•	General Medicine
•	Cardiology
•	Orthopedics
•	Pediatrics
•	ENT
•	Emergency
________________________________________
6.5 Queue Management
The system maintains patients in the correct order according to:
Priority → Token Number
For example:
Emergency Token 8
Emergency Token 12
Senior Citizen Token 3
Senior Citizen Token 7
Normal Token 1
Normal Token 2
________________________________________
6.6 Call Next Patient
The staff can select Call Next Patient.
The system automatically selects the highest-priority waiting patient.
A second patient cannot be called while another patient is currently In Progress.
________________________________________
6.7 Complete Consultation
After consultation, the staff can mark the patient's status as:
Completed
________________________________________
6.8 Cancel Token
A waiting or active token can be cancelled when required.
________________________________________
6.9 Queue Statistics
The system can display information such as:
•	Number of waiting patients
•	Patients currently being served
•	Completed consultations
•	Department-wise queue information
